# Blocks placed by hand are wired, selected and checked, each Wire is one undo step, and a Compile keeps them
place-block generator as g
place-block logic as l
place-block lamp as lamp
place-block power_display as p

wire-blocks g out to l a
expect-wire g out to l a
wire-blocks l out to lamp intensity
expect-wire l out to lamp intensity
expect-wires g 1
expect-wires l 2
expect-wires lamp 1
expect-wires p 0

# One undo takes one Wire off both blocks, and redo puts it back
undo
expect-wires l 1
expect-wires lamp 0
expect-wire g out to l a
redo
expect-wire l out to lamp intensity
expect-wires l 2

# An output feeds several inputs
wire-blocks l out to p x
expect-wires l 3

# What can't be wired
expect-step-fails wire-blocks nope out to l b because no block was placed or named as "nope"
expect-step-fails wire-blocks g out to nope a because no block was placed or named as "nope"
expect-step-fails wire-blocks g nope to l b because "g" has no output called 'nope'. Use out
expect-step-fails wire-blocks lamp out to l b because "lamp" has no output called 'out'
expect-step-fails wire-blocks g out to l nope because "l" has no input called 'nope'. Use a, b, op_in
expect-step-fails wire-blocks g out to l a because "l"'s input a already has a Wire
expect-step-fails wire-blocks p out to l a because "l"'s input a already has a Wire
expect-step-fails wire-blocks p out to l b because closes a Dependency Loop
expect-step-fails wire-blocks l out to l b because closes a Dependency Loop

# What a check finds wrong
expect-step-fails expect-wire g out to l b because no Wire g out to l b
expect-step-fails expect-wire g out to nope a because no block was placed or named as "nope"
expect-step-fails expect-wires l 2 because g out to l a
expect-step-fails expect-wires nope 2 because no block was placed or named as "nope"

# None of those changed a Wire
expect-wire g out to l a
expect-wires g 1
expect-wires l 3
expect-wires p 1

# A Delay makes a cycle that's no Dependency Loop
place-block delay as d
wire-blocks p out to d x
wire-blocks d out to l b
expect-wire d out to l b
expect-wires l 4

# An output's name follows the mode the block has in the level
place-block simple_telemetry as t
set-block-setting t mode global_velocity
expect-step-fails wire-blocks t speed to l op_in because "t" has no output called 'speed'
wire-blocks t heading to l op_in
expect-wire t heading to l op_in

# Selecting replaces the selection, and a wrong name leaves it as it was
select-blocks l p lamp
select-blocks lamp g
expect-step-fails select-blocks l nope because no block was placed or named as "nope"
open-window
new-script Inserted
insert-selected
expect-text lamp_1 = placed("
expect-text generator_1 = placed("
expect-step-fails expect-text logic_1 because the text doesn't contain it
expect-step-fails expect-text power_display_1 because the text doesn't contain it
screenshot selected

# A Compile that wires into a hand-wired block keeps the Wires it had
new-script Adds
set-text
lamp_1 = placed("{uid:lamp}")
lamp_1(red: 1)
end
compile
expect-result Placed 1 block
expect-wire l out to lamp intensity
expect-wires lamp 2

# keep-blocks leaves plain blocks wired, which wire by hand like the others
new-script Lights
set-text
power_display(1 & 1)
end
compile
expect-result Placed 3 blocks
name-group-block Lights logic as gate
name-group-block Lights power_display as display
expect-wire gate out to display x
expect-wires gate 3
open-delete Lights
press-prompt keep-blocks
expect-list-result kept its 3 blocks
expect-wire gate out to display x
expect-wires gate 3
wire-blocks g out to gate op_in
expect-wires gate 4
select-blocks gate display g
screenshot wired
expect-no-exceptions
